"hadiths[71]{hadithnumber,text}:"
1548,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever among you swears"
1549,Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:That Sa'd bin 'Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about a vow that was due from his mother
1550,"Salamah ibn Shabīb narrated to us, Abū al-Mughīrah narrated to us, from ʿUfayr ibn Maʿdān, from Sulaym ibn ʿĀmir, from Abū Umāmah (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The best sacrificial animal is the ram, and the best shroud is the *ḥullah* (a two-piece garment)."" Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a *gharīb* (uncommon) hadith, and ʿUfayr ibn Maʿdān is considered weak (*yuḍaʿʿaf*) in hadith transmission."
1551,"Narrated Abu Al-Bakhtari:""An Army from the armies of the Muslims"
1552,"Narrated Ibn 'Asim Al-Muzani:From his father and he was a Companion who said: ""When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) dispatched any army or battalion"
1553,"Narrated Anas:""When the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) set out for Khaibar"
1554,"Narrated Abu Talhah:""When the Prophet (ﷺ) overtook a people he would stay at the outskirts of their city for three nights"
1555,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) burnt the palm trees of Bani Nadir and cut them down at Al-Buwairah. So Allah revealed: Whatever you cut down of their palm trees"
1556,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The best companions are four"
1557,Narrated Yazid bin Hurmuz: That Najdah Al-Haruri wrote to Ibn 'Abbas asking if the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) would fight along with women
1558,"Narrated Abu Hurairah:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever among you swears"
1559,Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:That Sa'd bin 'Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about a vow that was due from his mother
1560,"Narrated by Qutaybah ibn Sa'id, from Malik ibn Anas, from Talhah ibn Abd al-Malik al-Ayli, from al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her), from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), who said:

""Whoever vows to obey Allah, let him obey Him; and whoever vows to disobey Allah, let him not disobey Him."""
1561,"Narrated Abu Musa: ""I arrived upon the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) at Khaibar along with a group of the Ash'ari tribe. He gave us shared along with those that conquered it."" This Hadith is Hasan Sahih Gharib. This is acted upon according to some of the people of knowledge. Al-Awza'i said: ""Whoever meets up with the Muslims before the horses"
1562,"Narrated Abu Sa’id Al Khudri : ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited selling the spoils of war until it has been distributed."" There is something on this topic from Abu Hurairah. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Gharib"
1563,Narrated Umm Habibah bint 'Irbad bin Sariyah: From her father who told her that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited intercourse with female prisoners
1564,"Narrated Abu Ayyub: That he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: ""Whoever separates between a mother and her child"
1565,"Narrated 'Ali: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said that Jibra'il had indeed descended upon him to say to him: ""Tell them - meaning your Companions - to choose regarding the captives of Badr"
1566,Narrated 'Imran bin Husain: That the Prophet (ﷺ) ransomed two men for the Muslims with a man from the idolaters. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. The paternal uncle of Abu Al-Muhallab's name is 'Abdur Rahman bin 'Amr
1567,Narrated Ibn 'Umar: That a woman was found killed in one of the expeditions of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)
1568,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas: ""I was informed by As-Sa'b bin Jaththamah who said: "" I said: ""O Messenger of Allah our horses trampled over women and children of the idolaters."" He said: ""They are from their fathers.'"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"
1569,"Narrated Abu Hurairah: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent us with an army and said: 'If you see so-and-so"
1570,"Narrated Thawban: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever dies and he is free of three: Kibr (Pride)"
1571,"Narrated Thawban:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever's soul departs from his body while he is free of three: Kanz (buried treasure)"
1572,"Narrated Simak Abu Rumail Al-Hanafi: ""I heard Ibn 'Abbas saying: 'Umar bin Al-Khattab narrated to me that he said: ""It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah! So-and-so has been martyred.' He said: ""No! I saw him in the fire of garment he pilfered from the spoils of war.' He said: 'Stand up O 'Umar! Call out that no one enters paradise except the believers.' Three times."" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih Gharib"
1573,"Narrated Anas: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to go to battle with Umm Sulaim"
1574,"Qutaybah narrated to us, that ʿAbd al-ʿAzīz ibn Muḥammad narrated to us, from al-ʿAlāʾ ibn ʿAbd al-Raḥmān, from his father, from Abū Hurayrah (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Do not make vows (nadhr), for a vow does not avert the divine decree in the least; it is only a means of extracting [wealth] from the miserly."" He (the narrator) said: In this chapter there is also a narration from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allāh be pleased with both of them). Abū ʿĪsā said: The ḥadīth of Abū Hurayrah is a ḥasan ḥadīth. The practice according to this is held by some of the people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and others, who disliked making vows. ʿAbdullāh ibn al-Mubārak said: The meaning of the dislike (karāhah) regarding vows applies to both acts of obedience and acts of disobedience. If a man makes a vow to perform an act of obedience and fulfills it, he shall receive reward for it, yet the act of vowing itself is disliked for him."
1575,Narrated 'Iyad bin Himar: That he gave the Prophet (ﷺ) a gift or a camel
1576,"Narrated Abu Bakrah: ""The Prophet (ﷺ) was met by some affair that made him happy"
1577,"Narrated Abu Al-Faid: ""I heard Sulaim bin 'Amir saying: 'There was a treaty between Mu'awiyah and the people of Rome. He was making an expedition into their lands so that when the period of the treaty was expires he would attack them. So when a man upon an animal' - or - 'upon a horse said: ""Allahu Akbar! Fulfillment not betrayal!"" - and it turned out to be 'Amr bin 'Abasah - Mu'awiyah asked him about that. He said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever has a treaty between himself and a people"
1578,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed the one who betrays will have a banner erected for him on the Day of Judgement."" [He said:] There are narrations on this topic from 'Ali"
1579,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Narrated by Thābit ibn al-Ḍaḥḥāk (may Allāh be pleased with him), who said:**

The Messenger of Allāh (peace and blessings be upon him) said:

> **""Whoever swears an oath by a religion other than Islām, while lying, then he is as he said.""**

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: *""This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith.""*

He further stated: *""The people of knowledge have differed regarding this matter. If a man swears by a religion other than Islām, saying, 'I am a Jew or a Christian if I do such and such,' and then he does that thing, some of them said: 'He has committed a grave sin, and there is no expiation (kaffārah) upon him.' This is the position of the people of Madīnah, and upon this Mālik ibn Anas ruled. Abū ʿUbayd also inclined toward this opinion.*

*And some of the people of knowledge among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), the Tābiʿūn, and others said: 'There is an expiation (kaffārah) upon him for that.' This is the position of Sufyān (al-Thawrī), Aḥmad, and Isḥāq (ibn Rāhawayh).""*

---

**Source:** Jāmiʿ al-Tirmidhī"
1580,"Narrated Samurah bin Jundab: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Kill the elder men among the idolaters and spare the Sharkh amont them."" And the Sharkh are the boys who did not begin to grow pubic hair. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. Hajjaj bin Artah narrated similarly from Qatadah"
1581,"Ishaq ibn Mansur narrated to us: Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: al-Awza'i narrated to us: al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever among you swears an oath and says in his oath, 'By al-Lat and al-'Uzza,' let him say, 'There is no god but Allah.' And whoever says, 'Come, let me gamble with you,' let him give in charity."" Abu 'Isa (al-Tirmidhi) said: This is a hasan sahih hadith. Abu al-Mughirah is al-Khawlani al-Himsi, and his name is 'Abd al-Quddus ibn al-Hajjaj."
1582,"Qutaybah narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from 'Ubayd Allah ibn 'Abd ibn 'Utbah, from Ibn 'Abbas, that Sa'd ibn 'Ubadah asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) about a vow that his mother had made but had passed away before fulfilling it. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Fulfill it on her behalf."" Abu 'Isa said: This is a hasan sahih hadith."
1583,"Muhammad ibn 'Abd al-A'la narrated to us: 'Imran ibn 'Uyaynah—he is the brother of Sufyan ibn 'Uyaynah—narrated to us, from Husayn, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Abu Umamah and other Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who said: ""Any Muslim man who frees a Muslim male slave shall be his ransom from the Fire; every limb of the freed slave shall be a ransom for a corresponding limb of the master. And any Muslim man who frees two Muslim female slaves shall be his ransom from the Fire; every limb of the two shall be a ransom for a corresponding limb of the master. And any Muslim woman who frees a Muslim female slave shall be her ransom from the Fire; every limb of the freed slave shall be a ransom for a corresponding limb of the mistress."" Abu 'Isa said: This is a hasan sahih gharib hadith from this chain. Abu 'Isa further commented: The hadith indicates that freeing male slaves is more meritorious than freeing female slaves, based on the Prophet’s statement: ""Whoever frees a Muslim male slave shall be his ransom from the Fire; every limb of his shall be a ransom for a limb of his."""
1584,"Narrated Simak Abu Rumail Al-Hanafi: ""I heard Ibn 'Abbas saying: 'Umar bin Al-Khattab narrated to me that he said: ""It was said: 'O Messenger of Allah! So-and-so has been martyred.' He said: ""No! I saw him in the fire of garment he pilfered from the spoils of war.' He said: 'Stand up O 'Umar! Call out that no one enters paradise except the believers.' Three times."" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih Gharib"
1585,"Narrated Anas: ""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) used to go to battle with Umm Sulaim"
1586,"Narrated by al-Ansari, narrated by Ma'n, narrated to me Malik ibn Anas, from Humayd, from Anas, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) set out for Khaybar, he arrived at night. Whenever he came to a people at night, he would not attack them until morning. When morning came, the Jews came out with their spades and baskets. When they saw him, they said, ""Muhammad and his army have come! By Allah, Muhammad has come with his army!"" The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allahu Akbar! Khaybar is ruined! Indeed, when we descend upon the courtyard of a people, evil is the morning of those who have been warned."""
1587,Narrated 'Iyad bin Himar: That he gave the Prophet (ﷺ) a gift or a camel
1588,"Narrated Abu Bakrah: ""The Prophet (ﷺ) was met by some affair that made him happy"
1589,Narrated Abu Hurairah:\n\nThat the Prophet (ﷺ) said: Indeed a woman grants (assurances of protection) to a people - meaning it is to be honored - from the Muslims. \n
1590,"Narrated Abu Hurayrah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet ﷺ said:

""I have been favoured over the prophets with six things: I have been given the jawāmiʿ al-kalim (the concise, comprehensive speech), I have been aided by terror (cast into the hearts of enemies), the spoils of war have been made lawful for me, the earth has been made for me a masjid (place of prayer) and a means of purification, I have been sent to all of creation, and the prophets have been sealed with me.""

This is a hasan sahih hadith."
1591,"and Al-Walid bin Rabah heard from Abu Hurairah, and he is Muqarib (average) in Hadith. \nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 1579 Arabic Hadees: 1579"""
1592,"Narrated Abu Al-Faid: ""I heard Sulaim bin 'Amir saying: 'There was a treaty between Mu'awiyah and the people of Rome. He was making an expedition into their lands so that when the period of the treaty was expires he would attack them. So when a man upon an animal' - or - 'upon a horse said: ""Allahu Akbar! Fulfillment not betrayal!"" - and it turned out to be 'Amr bin 'Abasah - Mu'awiyah asked him about that. He said: ""I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Whoever has a treaty between himself and a people"
1593,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed the one who betrays will have a banner erected for him on the Day of Judgement."" [He said:] There are narrations on this topic from 'Ali"
1594,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Qutaybah narrated to us; Ḥātim ibn Ismāʿīl narrated to us, from Jaʿfar ibn Muḥammad, from his father, from Yazīd ibn Hurmuz, that Najdah al-Ḥarūrī wrote to Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما asking him: ""Did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ take women along on military expeditions, and did he allocate a share of the war booty for them?""**

**Ibn ʿAbbās رضي الله عنهما wrote back to him: ""You have written to me asking whether the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to take women along on military expeditions. Indeed, he ﷺ would take them along, and they would tend to the wounded and would be given something from the booty as a gratuity (*yuḥdhayna*), but as for a designated share (*sahm*), he ﷺ did not allocate a fixed share for them.""**

**In this chapter, there are also narrations from Anas رضي الله عنه and Umm ʿAṭiyyah رضي الله عنها.**

**This is a *ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ* hadith. The practice according to the majority of the scholars is based upon this, and it is the position of Sufyān al-Thawrī and al-Shāfiʿī.**

**Some of them said: ""A share of the booty should be allocated for the woman and the child."" This is the position of al-Awzāʿī.**

**Al-Awzāʿī said: ""The Prophet ﷺ allocated shares for the boys at Khaybar, and the leaders of the Muslims allocated a share for every newborn born in the land of war.""**

**Al-Awzāʿī also said: ""The Prophet ﷺ allocated shares for the women at Khaybar, and the Muslims after him acted upon this.""**

**ʿAlī ibn Khashram narrated this to us; ʿĪsā ibn Yūnus narrated to us from al-Awzāʿī with this.**

**The meaning of his statement ""yuḥdhayna min al-ghanīmah"" is that they would be given something from the booty as a gratuity (*yuḍrakh lahunna*), i.e., they would be given a gift from it.**"
1595,"Narrated Samurah bin Jundab: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Kill the elder men among the idolaters and spare the Sharkh amont them."" And the Sharkh are the boys who did not begin to grow pubic hair. [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. Hajjaj bin Artah narrated similarly from Qatadah"
1596,"Narrated 'Atiyyah Al-Qurazi: ""We were presented to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on the day of (the battle of) Quraizah. Whoever had pubic hair was killed and whoever did not was left to his way. I was of those who did not have pubic hair so I was left to my way."" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. This is acted upon according to some of the people of knowledge. They consider pubic hair an indication of the age of responsibility"
1597,"It is narrated from al-Zuhri that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, allotted a share of the spoils of war to a group of Jews who fought alongside him. Qutaybah ibn Sa'id related this to us; 'Abd al-Warith ibn Sa'id informed us from 'Azrah ibn Thabit from al-Zuhri with this chain. This is a hasan gharib hadith."
1598,"Narrated Bajalah bin 'Abdah : ""I was a scribe for Jaz' bin Mu'awiyah at Manadhir when 'Umar's letter came to us (saying): 'Inspect the Zoroastrians around you to take the Jizyah from them. For indeed 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Awf informed me that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) took the Jizyah from the Zoroastrians of Hajar.'"" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan"
1599,"Narrated Bajalah: That 'Umar would not take the Jizyah from the Zoroastrians until 'Abdur-Rahman bin 'Awf informed him that the Prophet (ﷺ) took Jizyah from the Zoroastrians of Hajar."" There is more dialogue in the Hadith than this. And this Hadith is Hasan Sahih"
1600,"It was narrated to us that Hannad said: It was narrated to us by Ibn Al-Mubarak, from Haywah ibn Shurayh, who said: I heard Rabi'ah ibn Yazid Al-Dimashqi saying: Abu Idris Al-Khulani, 'A'idhullah ibn 'Ubaydullah, informed me that he heard Abu Tha'labah Al-Khushni saying: I came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah, we are in the land of a People of the Book, and we eat from their vessels."" He (ﷺ) said: ""If you find other vessels, do not eat from them. If you cannot find any, then wash them and eat from them."" Abu 'Isa (At-Tirmidhi) said: This is a Hasan (good) and Sahih (authentic) Hadith."
1601,"Narrated 'Uqbah bin 'Amir: ""I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! We come across a people and they do not host us"
1602,"# Translation of the Hadith

**Hannād narrated to us** — Ibn Abī az-Zinād narrated to us, from his father, from ʿUbaydullāh ibn ʿAbdullāh ibn ʿUtbah, from Ibn ʿAbbāṣ (may Allāh be pleased with them both), that the Prophet ﷺ took as his personal spoil (*tanaffala*) his sword Dhū al-Faqār on the day of Badr, and it was the same sword regarding which he saw a vision on the day of Uḥud.

This is a *ḥasan gharīb* hadith. We only know it through this chain of narration, from the hadith of Ibn Abī az-Zinād.

The scholars have differed regarding the granting of a bonus share (*nafl*) from the one-fifth (*khums*). Mālik ibn Anas said: ""It has not reached me that the Messenger of Allāh ﷺ granted a bonus share in all of his military expeditions; however, it has reached me that he granted a bonus share in some of them. That was a matter of independent reasoning (*ijtihād*) on the part of the Imām, whether at the beginning of the war spoils or at the end.""

Ibn Manṣūr said: ""I said to Aḥmad: 'The Prophet ﷺ would grant a bonus share of one-fourth after the one-fifth when departing, and one-third after the one-fifth upon returning.'"" He (Aḥmad) said: ""He would extract the one-fifth first, then grant a bonus share from what remained, and he would not exceed this.""

Abū ʿĪsā (at-Tirmidhī) said: ""This hadith is in accordance with what Ibn al-Musayyib said — that the bonus share (*nafl*) is from the one-fifth (*khums*)."" Isḥāq said the same."
1603,"# Hadith Translation

**Narrated Abu Qatada (may Allah be pleased with him):**

The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said:

**""Whoever kills an enemy combatant for whom there is clear proof (of being a lawful target in battle), then his spoils of war (salab) shall be his.""**

---

**Imam Abu Isa (may Allah have mercy upon him) said:** *""And in the Hadith there is a longer narrative (story).""*

---

## Scholarly Notes:

- **"
1604,"Narrated Yazid bin Abi 'Ubaid: ""I said to Salamah bin Al-Akwa': ""For what did you pledge to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) on the Day of Al-Hudaibiyyah?"" He said: ""For death."" This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"
1605,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar: ""We used to pledge to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) to hear and obey."" So he would say to us: ""As much as you are able."" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih"
1606,"Narrated Jabir bin ‘Abdullah : ""We did not pledge to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) for death"
1607,"Narrated Abu Hurairah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Three will not be spoken to by Allah on the Day of Judgement"
1608,"Narrated Jabir: ""A slave came to give the pledge to the Prophet (ﷺ) for Hijrah"
1609,"Ibn Al-Munkadir heard Umaimah bin Ruqaiqah saying:""I pledged to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) along with some women. He said to us: 'In as much as you are able and capable.' I said: 'Allah and His Messenger are more merciful to us than we are to ourselves"
1610,"Narrated Al-Bara' : ""We used to say that the participants of Badr on the Day of Badr were like the number of companions of Talut"
1611,"Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\n\nThat the Prophet (ﷺ) said to a delegation from 'Abdul-Qais: I order you to give the Khumus from your spoils of war. \n\nHe said: There is a story with this Hadith\n\n[Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih. \nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 1599 Arabic Hadees: 1599"""
1612,"Narrated by Ibn Abi 'Umar, narrated by Sufyan, narrated by Ayyub, from Abu Qilabah, from his uncle, from Imran ibn Husayn, that the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, ransomed two Muslim men in exchange for one polytheist.

Abu 'Isa said: This is a hasan sahih hadith. The uncle of Abu Qilabah is Abu al-Muhallab, whose name is 'Abd al-Rahman ibn 'Amr, and it is also said Mu'awiyah ibn 'Amr. Abu Qilabah's name is 'Abd Allah ibn Zayd al-Jarmi.

The practice according to the majority of the scholars among the Companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, and others is that the Imam may grant freedom to whomever he wishes among the captives, kill whomever he wishes among them, and ransom whomever he wishes.

Some scholars preferred killing over ransom. Al-Awza'i said: ""It has reached me that this verse is abrogated — His Most High's words: 'Then either grant freedom afterward or ransom' — and it was abrogated by: 'And kill them wherever you find them.'""

We were informed of that by Hannad, narrated by Ibn al-Mubarak, from al-Awza'i.

Ishaq ibn Mansur said: I asked Ahmad: ""When a captive is taken, should he be killed or ransomed — which do you prefer?"" He said: ""If they are able to ransom him, there is no harm in that. And if he is killed, I know of no harm in that either.""

Ishaq ibn Ibrahim said: ""Killing is more beloved to me, unless the captive is well-known, in which case I hope to obtain much [benefit] through him."""
1613,"Narrated Anas: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever plunders then he is not of us."" [Abu 'Eisa said:] This Hadith is Hasan Sahih Gharib as a Hadith of Anas"
1614,"Narrated Abu Hurairah: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Do not precede the Jews and the Christians with the Salam. And if one you meets one of them in the path"
1615,"Narrated Ibn 'Umar: That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed when a Jew gives Salam to one of you"
1616,Narrated Qais bin Abu Hazim: From Jarir bin 'Abdullah that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) sent a military expedition to Khath'am. So some people (living there) sought safety by prostrating
1617,"Narrated Qais bin Abu Hazim: Similar to the narration of Abu Mu'aqiyah (no. 1604) but he did not mention in it: ""from Jarir"" in it"
1618,"Narrated 'Umar bin Al-Khattab:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""If I live - if Allah wills - I will expel the Jews and the Christians from the Arabian Peninsula"
